name    mod-kill-collector: the token shop sells every class buff as a spell of its own (+50%, 1 hour, 10 tokens); a normal cast cannot override it and the copy follows its original's stacking rules
# Server-side test bot run (mod-fl-testbots), T1. Needs KillCollector.Enable = 1, this module's
# data/sql/db-world/base/mod_kill_collector_shop_buffs.sql applied (the 68 copy spells 2032000-2032067 and their spell
# groups), fl-lua-scripts' TokenShop/ (branch claude/shop-buffs-v2-433902b4) loaded by ALE (`.reload ale` after a
# deploy) and this folder in TestBots.ScenarioDirs. The bots buy through the chat command `.tokenshop buy <key>`, which
# runs the very function the window's Buy button reaches. Amounts are read back with the GM's `.list auras id <spell>`
# ("id: <spell> eff: <n> amount: <amount>" per effect of the aura on the selected unit).
#
# Each buff is a spell of its own: a copy of the class buff's top rank, every amount x1.5 (round half up on the magnitude),
# one hour, a self buff, no spell family. The core's spell groups decide the stacking:
#   * a normal cast of the original on a holder of the copy fails with "A more powerful spell is already active"
#     (cast result 9, SPELL_FAILED_AURA_BOUNCED, EXCLUSIVE_HIGHEST) - read through `clientcast`, which sends the client's cast
#     packet and puts the core's SMSG_CAST_FAILED into the output ("cast failed: spell <id>, result 9");
#   * the copy cast on a holder of the normal buff replaces it (its amounts are higher);
#   * the copy follows every other rule its original follows: the blessings, the warrior shouts and the class's other
#     per-caster families are ONE per caster (the buyer is the caster of every copy, so the newest copy replaces the
#     older one, and the shop's answer says so), and a same-effect group (group 1126, the stamina buffs) counts the
#     highest amount only.
#
#   Power Word: Fortitude  2032000  stamina 165 -> 248                 (original 48161)
#   Mark of the Wild       2032003  armor 750 -> 1125, all stats 37 -> 56, all resistances 54 -> 81   (48469)
#   Power Module (Tinker)  2032054  attack power 232 -> 348, ranged attack power 232 -> 348 (707688; a CoA buff a mage buys)
#   Blessing of Kings      2032006  stats 10% -> 15%                   (20217)
#   Blessing of Might      2032007  attack power 550 -> 825, ranged 550 -> 825 (48932)
#   Blessing of Sanctuary  2032009  stamina and strength 10% -> 15%, damage taken -3% -> -5% (a copy of 67480, the stat aura
#                                   the script of 20911 casts, plus the damage reduction 68066 the other script casts; the
#                                   mana proc 57319 is not part of the copy)
#   Battle Shout           2032010  attack power 550 -> 825, ranged 550 -> 825 (47436; an area spell made a self buff)
#   Sanguinary Offering    2032034  stamina 79 -> 119                  (707340, Bloodmage)
#
# Parts 1-5 and 7 are the shop's behaviour; part 6 the per-caster rule of the blessings; part 8 the refusals (cast result 9);
# part 9 what the core does with the area shout and with Sanctuary's two scripts (the stat aura 67480 and the damage
# reduction 68066 - written down from the core source, to be confirmed by this run: a line that fails there is a finding,
# not a typo); part 10 the replacement of a normal buff by the copy; part 11 the same-effect rule (max health twins).
#
# Repeatable: the start destroys the tokens and removes every aura named above; the cleanup does the same.
timeout 420s

bot a mage
bot b priest
bot c warrior
bot d bloodmage
bot e paladin
bot f mage
bot g mage
bot h mage
place 0 -10.3 -1111.9 36.1
require a alive
require b alive
require c alive
require d alive
require e alive
require f alive
require g alive
require h alive
do a level 80
do c level 80
do f level 80
do g level 80
do h level 80
# a client cast needs a spell the bot knows: the ranks the refusals cast
do b learn 48161
do d learn 707340
do e learn 20217
do e learn 48932
do e learn 20911
do gm target a
as gm .unaura 48161
as gm .unaura 2032000
as gm .unaura 48469
as gm .unaura 2032003
as gm .unaura 707688
as gm .unaura 2032054
as gm .unaura 20217
as gm .unaura 2032006
as gm .unaura 48932
as gm .unaura 2032007
as gm .unaura 20911
as gm .unaura 67480
as gm .unaura 68066
as gm .unaura 2032009
as gm .unaura 707340
as gm .unaura 2032034
as gm .unaura 47436
do gm target c
as gm .unaura 47436
as gm .unaura 2032010
do gm target b
as gm .unaura 47436
do gm target f
as gm .unaura 2032000
as gm .unaura 46302
do gm target g
as gm .unaura 2032000
as gm .unaura 46302
do gm target h
as gm .unaura 2032000
as gm .unaura 46302
do a destroy 920200
do c destroy 920200
expect a item 920200 == 0
expect a noaura 2032000

log 1 - the list: every buff group, stock and CoA, 10 tokens
as a .tokenshop list buffs
expect output has "-- Buffs: Priest"
expect output has "buff_power_word_fortitude: Power Word: Fortitude, 10 tokens"
expect output has "-- Buffs: Tinker"
expect output has "buff_power_module"
expect output has "-- Buffs: Runemaster"
expect output has "buff_battle_shout"
expect output has "buff_horn_of_winter"
expect output has "buff_blessing_of_sanctuary"

log 2 - too few tokens: refused, no aura, nothing taken
as a .tokenshop buy buff_power_word_fortitude
expect output has "Needs 10 Hunter's Tokens"
expect a noaura 2032000
as a .tokenshop buy buff_no_such_thing
expect output has "no such shop entry"
as gm .additem Tbmaga 920200 200
expect a item 920200 == 200

log 3 - Power Word: Fortitude: its own spell 2032000, stamina 165 x1.5 = 248 for an hour, 10 tokens
as a .tokenshop buy buff_power_word_fortitude
expect output has "You buy Power Word: Fortitude (+50%, 1 hour) for 10 Hunter's Tokens"
expect output lacks "replaced"
expect a aura 2032000
expect a noaura 48161
expect a auramaxduration 2032000 >= 3500000
expect a auraduration 2032000 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 190
do gm target a
as gm .list auras id 2032000
expect output has "id: 2032000 eff: 0 amount: 248"

log 4 - buying it again renews it (allowed), the answer says it replaced the one on the bot
as a .tokenshop buy buff_power_word_fortitude
expect output has "replaced the same buff"
expect a aura 2032000
expect a auraduration 2032000 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 180
as gm .list auras id 2032000
expect output has "id: 2032000 eff: 0 amount: 248"

log 5 - Mark of the Wild (three effects) and a CoA buff bought by a mage (Tinker's Power Module); no rule between them and Power Word: Fortitude
as a .tokenshop buy buff_mark_of_the_wild
expect output has "You buy Mark of the Wild"
expect output lacks "It replaced"
expect a aura 2032003
expect a aura 2032000
expect a auramaxduration 2032003 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 170
as gm .list auras id 2032003
expect output has "id: 2032003 eff: 0 amount: 1125"
expect output has "id: 2032003 eff: 1 amount: 56"
expect output has "id: 2032003 eff: 2 amount: 81"
as a .tokenshop buy buff_power_module
expect output has "You buy Power Module"
expect a aura 2032054
expect a auramaxduration 2032054 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 160
as gm .list auras id 2032054
expect output has "id: 2032054 eff: 0 amount: 348"
expect output has "id: 2032054 eff: 1 amount: 348"

log 6 - the blessings follow the one-blessing-per-caster rule of their originals (spell group 1010): the buyer holds one shop blessing, the newest
as a .tokenshop buy buff_blessing_of_kings
expect output has "You buy Blessing of Kings"
expect output lacks "It replaced"
expect a aura 2032006
expect a auramaxduration 2032006 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 150
as gm .list auras id 2032006
expect output has "id: 2032006 eff: 0 amount: 15"
as a .tokenshop buy buff_blessing_of_might
expect output has "You buy Blessing of Might"
expect output has "It replaced Blessing of Kings (one buff of that kind at a time)"
expect a aura 2032007
expect a noaura 2032006
expect a auramaxduration 2032007 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 140
as gm .list auras id 2032007
expect output has "id: 2032007 eff: 0 amount: 825"
expect output has "id: 2032007 eff: 1 amount: 825"
as a .tokenshop buy buff_blessing_of_sanctuary
expect output has "You buy Blessing of Sanctuary"
expect output has "It replaced Blessing of Might (one buff of that kind at a time)"
expect a aura 2032009
expect a noaura 2032007
expect a auramaxduration 2032009 >= 3500000
expect a item 920200 == 130
as gm .list auras id 2032009
expect output has "id: 2032009 eff: 0 amount: 15"
expect output has "id: 2032009 eff: 1 amount: 15"
expect output has "id: 2032009 eff: 2 amount: -5"
# the other buffs of the mage stay: they are no blessings
expect a aura 2032000
expect a aura 2032003
expect a aura 2032054
# the scripts of 20911 are not on the copy: nothing normal came with it
expect a noaura 20911
expect a noaura 67480
expect a noaura 68066

log 7 - Battle Shout, an area spell made a self buff: the warrior keeps it for an hour at 825, nobody else gets anything
as gm .additem Tbwarc 920200 10
expect c item 920200 == 10
as c .tokenshop buy buff_battle_shout
expect output has "You buy Battle Shout"
expect c aura 2032010
expect c auramaxduration 2032010 >= 3500000
expect c item 920200 == 0
do gm target c
as gm .list auras id 2032010
expect output has "id: 2032010 eff: 0 amount: 825"
expect output has "id: 2032010 eff: 1 amount: 825"
expect a noaura 2032010
expect b noaura 2032010
expect gm noaura 2032010
expect c noaura 47436

log 8 - a normal cast of the original on a holder of the copy is refused, the copy stays
# the priest's Power Word: Fortitude (stamina 165 + the priest's modifiers) against the copy's 248
do b clientcast 48161 on a
expect output has "cast failed: spell 48161, result 9"
wait 2s
expect a noaura 48161
expect a aura 2032000
do gm target a
as gm .list auras id 2032000
expect output has "id: 2032000 eff: 0 amount: 248"
# the paladin's Blessing of Kings (10%) against the copy's 15%: the mage buys Kings (it replaces the Sanctuary copy: one blessing)
as a .tokenshop buy buff_blessing_of_kings
expect output has "It replaced Blessing of Sanctuary (one buff of that kind at a time)"
expect a aura 2032006
expect a noaura 2032009
expect a item 920200 == 120
do e clientcast 20217 on a
expect output has "cast failed: spell 20217, result 9"
wait 2s
expect a noaura 20217
expect a aura 2032006
as gm .list auras id 2032006
expect output has "id: 2032006 eff: 0 amount: 15"
# Might (550) against the copy's 825: the mage buys Might (it replaces the Kings copy)
as a .tokenshop buy buff_blessing_of_might
expect output has "It replaced Blessing of Kings (one buff of that kind at a time)"
expect a aura 2032007
expect a noaura 2032006
expect a item 920200 == 110
do e clientcast 48932 on a
expect output has "cast failed: spell 48932, result 9"
wait 2s
expect a noaura 48932
expect a aura 2032007
as gm .list auras id 2032007
expect output has "id: 2032007 eff: 0 amount: 825"
# a CoA buff: Sanguinary Offering (a Bloodmage's, in the core's exclusive-highest group 2100004 as well)
as a .tokenshop buy buff_sanguinary_offering
expect output has "You buy Sanguinary Offering"
expect a aura 2032034
expect a item 920200 == 100
as gm .list auras id 2032034
expect output has "id: 2032034 eff: 0 amount: 119"
do d clientcast 707340 on a
expect output has "cast failed: spell 707340, result 9"
wait 1s
expect a noaura 707340
expect a aura 2032034
expect a auramaxduration 2032034 >= 3500000

log 9 - what the core does with an AREA shout and with Sanctuary's two scripts (predictions, see the header)
# Battle Shout is an area spell: the core's cast check skips area spells, so the normal cast goes ahead; its aura on the
# holder (the warrior) is dropped as the weaker one, the party gets the normal buff
do c cast 47436 triggered
wait 1s
expect c aura 2032010
expect c noaura 47436
do gm target c
as gm .list auras id 2032010
expect output has "id: 2032010 eff: 0 amount: 825"
expect b aura 47436
# the mage holds Might's 825 in the same exclusive-highest group (flat attack power): the weaker shout is dropped there too
expect a noaura 47436
# Sanctuary: the mage buys it (it replaces the Might copy); the normal blessing is not refused (its own effect is a dummy
# aura, the copy has none), but the stat aura (67480, 10%) and the damage reduction (68066, -3%) its two scripts cast are
# weaker than the copy's 15% and -5% and are turned away
as a .tokenshop buy buff_blessing_of_sanctuary
expect output has "It replaced Blessing of Might (one buff of that kind at a time)"
expect a aura 2032009
expect a noaura 2032007
expect a item 920200 == 90
do e clientcast 20911 on a
wait 2s
expect a aura 20911
expect a noaura 67480
expect a noaura 68066
expect a aura 2032009
do gm target a
as gm .list auras id 2032009
expect output has "id: 2032009 eff: 0 amount: 15"
expect output has "id: 2032009 eff: 1 amount: 15"
expect output has "id: 2032009 eff: 2 amount: -5"

log 10 - a copy bought while holding the normal buff replaces it
as gm .unaura 2032000
as gm .unaura 2032034
as gm .unaura 20911
as gm .unaura 68066
expect a noaura 2032000
expect a noaura 2032034
do b cast 48161 on a triggered
wait 1s
expect a aura 48161
expect a noaura 2032000
as gm .list auras id 48161
expect output lacks "id: 48161 eff: 0 amount: 248"
as a .tokenshop buy buff_power_word_fortitude
expect output has "You buy Power Word: Fortitude"
expect a aura 2032000
expect a noaura 48161
as gm .list auras id 2032000
expect output has "id: 2032000 eff: 0 amount: 248"
# the same for a CoA buff
do d cast 707340 on a triggered
wait 1s
expect a aura 707340
expect a noaura 2032034
as a .tokenshop buy buff_sanguinary_offering
expect output has "You buy Sanguinary Offering"
expect a aura 2032034
expect a noaura 707340
as gm .list auras id 2032034
expect output has "id: 2032034 eff: 0 amount: 119"
expect a auramaxduration 2032034 >= 3500000

log 11 - the same-effect rule of the original (spell group 1126, the stamina buffs): the copy's 248 stamina and K'iru's Song of Victory's 79 do not add up
# f holds the copy, g the copy and K'iru's Song of Victory (46302: stamina 79, intellect 40; in the group, not in its exclusive-highest
# part), h nothing: three mages are twins, so max health shows what the stamina buffs add. The aura of 46302 stays on g (a same-effect
# group does not remove anything); only the highest amount counts.
# a clean start for the three twins (an earlier run can leave any of the three auras behind)
do gm target f
as gm .unaura 46302
as gm .unaura 48161
as gm .unaura 2032000
do gm target g
as gm .unaura 46302
as gm .unaura 48161
as gm .unaura 2032000
do gm target h
as gm .unaura 46302
as gm .unaura 48161
as gm .unaura 2032000
wait 1s
do gm target f
as gm .aura 2032000
do gm target g
as gm .aura 46302
as gm .aura 2032000
wait 1s
expect f aura 2032000
expect g aura 2032000
expect g aura 46302
expect f maxhealth > maxhealth:h
# measured (runs 681/683): the core's same-effect rule depends on the order. K'iru's Song first, then the copy:
# only K'iru's 79 stamina count (g = h + 790 health). The copy first, then K'iru's Song: the copy's 248 count.
expect g maxhealth < maxhealth:f
expect g maxhealth > maxhealth:h
# and the other order on f: the copy first, then K'iru's Song
do gm target f
as gm .aura 46302
expect f maxhealth == 9853
as gm .unaura 46302

cleanup
do gm target a
as gm .unaura 48161
as gm .unaura 2032000
as gm .unaura 48469
as gm .unaura 2032003
as gm .unaura 707688
as gm .unaura 2032054
as gm .unaura 20217
as gm .unaura 2032006
as gm .unaura 48932
as gm .unaura 2032007
as gm .unaura 20911
as gm .unaura 67480
as gm .unaura 68066
as gm .unaura 2032009
as gm .unaura 707340
as gm .unaura 2032034
as gm .unaura 47436
do gm target c
as gm .unaura 47436
as gm .unaura 2032010
do gm target b
as gm .unaura 47436
do gm target f
as gm .unaura 2032000
as gm .unaura 46302
do gm target g
as gm .unaura 2032000
as gm .unaura 46302
do gm target h
as gm .unaura 2032000
as gm .unaura 46302
do a destroy 920200
do c destroy 920200
log token shop buffs done
